WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.448
In the thirteenth century, a young Venetian merchant named Marco Polo came to China.

00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:14.054
After a long journey, he finally set foot on this unfamiliar land.

00:00:14.404 --> 00:00:19.492
He met Kublai Khan, the emperor of the Yuan dynasty, and received a warm welcome.

00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:27.402
Marco Polo saw prosperous cities, wide roads and bustling markets.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:32.624
He looked curiously at everything in the streets; it all felt new to him.

00:00:32.974 --> 00:00:38.446
He lived in China for many years and traveled to very many places.

00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:43.740
After returning to Europe, he wrote down what he had seen and heard as The Travels of Marco Polo.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:49.130
Sitting at his desk, he carefully wrote down everything he had seen along the way.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:55.528
This book filled many Europeans with a deep interest in the mysterious East.

00:00:55.878 --> 00:01:00.870
From then on, even more Europeans began to long for the far-off East.

